CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ qualified explicit specialization selected: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ primary template used for non-specialized arg: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.expl.spec]/2: an explicit class template specialization may be named
with a qualified-id from an enclosing namespace (template <> struct ns::G<char>).
CBMC previously silently skipped such a specialization (treating it like an
out-of-class nested definition) and used the primary template, which also breaks
specializing std::hash for a user type outside namespace std.  assertion.3
FAILURE proves non-vacuity.
